From aaa0a4e6460d56d1c412473f95cd204e84a66f2f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gaia <build@heygaia.io>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 04:23:45 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(layout): a native form control measures to its intrinsic
 size instead of flooring min-height

Patch 0004 kept a stretched grid-item control from collapsing to 0px by
overwriting its min-height with its rows/size intrinsic height. That
replaced the author's min-height (min-height:0 included) and outgrew a fixed
track the control should have been stretched to: a rows=3 textarea in a 10px
row laid out 60px tall instead of 10px.

A native control (input, select, textarea) is now a layout leaf that
measures to its intrinsic content size, with no aspect ratio, so an auto axis
that alignment stretches contributes that size to an auto track the way
taffy's grid algorithm handles any content, and the author's min and max
sizes apply as written. Its descendants (options, a textarea's text) are its
value and were never boxes in its layout.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tm2SNEJ42hMPiZ6cFb8Vih
